  pages:
  - Outstanding work. The dish in front of you carries a layered and partly open
    history.
  - 'Outstanding work. The dish in front of you carries a layered and partly open
    history. '
  - '.The beef came from Spanish era cattle ranching. '
  - The bagoong alamang comes from pre-Hispanic Filipino fermentation.
  - 'Whether the specific assembly came from the Kapampangan domestic kitchen, '
  - ' from Indian sepoys who settled in Cainta after 1764, or from Mexican mole traditions
    is still argued by scholars today.'
  - Not every culinary question has a clean answer. Some of the most interesting
